# Model card for mms-tts-tel (Telugu)

* Source: https://huggingface.co/facebook/mms-tts (models/tel), Meta Massively Multilingual Speech (MMS), repo sha `44cc7fb408064ef9ea6e7c59130d88cac1274671` (same commit used for the Bengali voice).
* License: CC BY-NC 4.0 (non-commercial) - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
* Attribution: Meta MMS-TTS (facebook/mms-tts, tel), converted to ONNX for sherpa-onnx (character frontend, no espeak).
* Language: tel (Telugu), 1 speaker, sample rate 16,000 Hz.
* Converted with sherpa-onnx's documented vits-mms.py (tts-research/mms-tel/MMS_TEL_CONVERSION.md); the HiFi-GAN
  decoder was then converted to fp16 with the same script used for Bengali
  (tts-research/mms-ben/speed/mms_decoder_fp16.py; encoder, duration predictor and flow stay fp32). Quality UNVERIFIED.
* Text normalisation in the app (TeluguTextNormalizer): digits (Telugu ౦-౯ and ASCII) -> Telugu number words
  (AI4Bharat indic-numtowords 1.1.0 data, MIT, tel/cardinal.py ported to Kotlin). Unicode NFC. The ASCII period and
  ZWNJ (U+200C) are not in the vocabulary and are dropped, unchanged from the model's own behaviour.
